The results for each situation and rule, and what real AI reading changed. With real AI reading and "only the guest", the allergen went out in 4 (Decisions), 0 (picking options), 0 (writing names) of 300 orders. Under "anyone", staff saying "actually, it's fine" was taken as a correction: Decisions 7, picking options 19, writing names 10 (of 120). Allergies said once and read as "not mentioned": Decisions 4, picking options 0, writing names 0 (of 300).

34
00:02:26,067 --> 00:02:32,067
Just ask the guest? A second new test: 240 orders. Staff say a recorded allergy is fine. A new rule: the system texts the guest "Does anyone need to avoid it?" and only the guest's answer can cancel the allergy.

